        <body>
            <div xml:id="d43">

                <pb facs="0194" n="94" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg94"/>

                <head>No. 43.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Young
                        to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-04-16"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 16, 1884.</date>
                        (Received June 23.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 427]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: As a further reference to my dispatch No.
                    407, of March. 31, I have the honor to transmit herewith, for the information of
                    the Department, a copy of a dispatch from Mr. Consul Seymour, at Canton, showing
                        <pb facs="0195" n="95" xml:id="pg95"/> the temper of the people and the
                    condition of affairs in Southern China.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN RUSSELL YOUNG.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d43-a1.xml" xpointer="d43-a1"/>
            </div>
